\f0\fs24 \cf0 ============================================================\
                    PROJECTCOLLAB\
       STUDENT PROJECT COLLABORATION PLATFORM\
============================================================\
\
1. PROJECT OVERVIEW\
-------------------\
\
Project Name: ProjectCollab\
\
Project Type: Full-Stack Web Application\
\
Domain: Education, Student Collaboration, Team Formation\
\
Target Users: College Students\
\
ProjectCollab is a college-specific student project collaboration\
platform that enables students from the same college to discover\
projects, find teammates, recruit collaborators, and work together.\
\
Students can publish project ideas, specify the skills and roles\
they require, and invite other students to apply.\
\
Other students can browse available projects, explore opportunities\
matching their interests, and apply to join teams.\
\
The project owner can review applications and accept or reject\
applicants. Once accepted, students become team members and can use\
the platform's collaboration features.\
\
The platform also helps students who need partners for academic\
projects, including mini-projects, major projects, research projects,\
and hackathons.\
\
The initial version will focus on students from a single college.\
Support for multiple colleges can be introduced in the future.\
\
\
2. PROBLEM STATEMENT\
--------------------\
\
Students frequently face difficulties finding suitable teammates\
for academic and personal projects.\
\
The main problems include:\
\
1. Students' interests may differ from those of their friends.\
\
2. A student interested in AI/ML, cybersecurity, robotics, or another\
   specialized field may not find interested teammates in their\
   existing friend circle.\
\
3. Students working on major university projects may struggle to\
   find reliable partners.\
\
4. Students with useful technical skills may not know about projects\
   that need their contribution.\
\
5. Students with project ideas may not know where to recruit people\
   with the required skills.\
\
6. Students without project ideas may still want to participate in\
   projects and gain practical experience.\
\
7. Finding teammates through informal college groups can be\
   disorganized and time-consuming.\
\
ProjectCollab addresses these problems by providing a centralized\
platform for project discovery, recruitment, and collaboration.\
\
\
3. PROJECT OBJECTIVES\
---------------------\
\
The primary objectives are:\
\
1. Provide a centralized platform for college students to discover\
   and create projects.\
\
2. Help students find teammates based on skills and interests.\
\
3. Allow project owners to publish project requirements and recruit\
   suitable collaborators.\
\
4. Implement an application management system with accept and\
   reject functionality.\
\
5. Help students find partners for mini-projects, major projects,\
   research, and competitions.\
\
6. Provide student profiles displaying skills, interests, and\
   previous projects.\
\
7. Provide basic collaboration tools for accepted team members.\
\
8. Encourage practical learning and interdisciplinary collaboration.\
\
9. Build a secure, responsive, and maintainable web application.\
\
10. Create a foundation for future recommendation and team-matching\
    functionality.\
\
\
4. TARGET USERS\
---------------\
\
A. Students with Project Ideas\
\
Students who have an idea but need additional team members.\
\
B. Students Looking for Projects\
\
Students who want to join projects based on their interests,\
skills, and learning goals.\
\
C. Students Looking for Major Project Partners\
\
Students who need partners for university academic projects.\
\
D. Students Looking for Practical Experience\
\
Students who want to improve their skills by contributing to\
projects outside their existing friend circle.\
\
E. Platform Administrators\
\
Authorized administrators responsible for managing users,\
moderating content, and maintaining the college community.\
\
\
5. TECHNOLOGY STACK\
-------------------\
\
FRONTEND\
\
1. React.js\
   Used to build interactive user interfaces and reusable components.\
\
2. JavaScript\
   Used for frontend functionality, event handling, and API requests.\
\
3. HTML5\
   Provides the structure of web pages.\
\
4. CSS3\
   Used for layouts, styling, responsiveness, and animations.\
\
5. Tailwind CSS\
   Optional utility-first CSS framework for consistent UI styling.\
\
6. React Router\
   Used for navigation between pages.\
\
7. Axios or Fetch API\
   Used to communicate with the backend.\
\
BACKEND\
\
1. Node.js\
   JavaScript runtime used to execute server-side code.\
\
2. Express.js\
   Backend framework used to create REST APIs and process requests.\
\
3. JavaScript\
   Used to implement business logic, authentication middleware,\
   validation, and application workflows.\
\
DATABASE\
\
1. PostgreSQL\
   Relational database used to store users, projects, applications,\
   team members, tasks, and notifications.\
\
2. pg\
   Node.js PostgreSQL client for database connectivity.\
\
AUTHENTICATION AND SECURITY\
\
1. bcrypt\
   Used to hash passwords if password authentication is implemented\
   directly in the backend.\
\
2. JSON Web Tokens (JWT)\
   Optional approach for managing authenticated API sessions.\
\
3. Express middleware\
   Used for authentication, authorization, and request validation.\
\
4. Helmet\
   Helps configure security-related HTTP headers.\
\
5. Rate limiting\
   Helps reduce abuse of authentication and other sensitive endpoints.\
\
DEVELOPMENT TOOLS\
\
1. Visual Studio Code\
   Code editor.\
\
2. Git\
   Version control.\
\
3. GitHub\
   Source code repository and collaboration.\
\
4. Postman\
   API testing.\
\
5. npm\
   Package management.\
\
DEPLOYMENT\
\
1. Vercel\
   Suitable for deploying the React frontend.\
\
2. A Node.js-compatible hosting service\
   Used to deploy the Express backend.\
\
3. A managed PostgreSQL service\
   Used to host the production database.\
\
The frontend, backend, and database may be hosted separately.\
\
IMPORTANT:\
Use environment variables for database credentials, authentication\
secrets, and other sensitive configuration.\
\
Never commit secrets or production credentials to GitHub.\
\
\
6. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE\
----------------------\
\
The application will follow a client-server architecture.\
\
USER\
 |\
 v\
REACT FRONTEND\
 |\
 | HTTP Requests / REST API\
 v\
NODE.JS + EXPRESS BACKEND\
 |\
 | Authentication, Authorization,\
 | Validation, Business Logic\
 v\
POSTGRESQL DATABASE\
 |\
 v\
STORED APPLICATION DATA\
\
\
FRONTEND RESPONSIBILITIES\
\
- Display pages and dashboards.\
- Collect user input.\
- Display projects and profiles.\
- Submit applications.\
- Show application statuses.\
- Display notifications.\
- Provide task and team interfaces.\
\
BACKEND RESPONSIBILITIES\
\
- Authenticate users.\
- Verify permissions.\
- Create and update projects.\
- Process project applications.\
- Manage team membership.\
- Enforce recruitment rules.\
- Generate notifications.\
- Validate requests.\
- Communicate with PostgreSQL.\
\
DATABASE RESPONSIBILITIES\
\
- Store user information.\
- Store college and skill information.\
- Store project listings.\
- Store applications and their statuses.\
- Store team membership.\
- Store tasks and notifications.\
- Maintain relationships and constraints.\
\
\
7. CORE MODULES\
----------------\
\
MODULE 1: AUTHENTICATION AND AUTHORIZATION\
\
Purpose:\
Provide secure access to the platform.\
\
Features:\
\
- Student registration.\
- Student login.\
- Logout.\
- Password hashing.\
- Forgot-password functionality.\
- Email verification.\
- Protected pages.\
- Role-based access control.\
- College membership validation.\
\
User roles:\
\
1. Student\
2. Platform Administrator\
\
Project owners receive additional permissions for the projects\
they manage.\
\
College Verification:\
\
The initial release should support one college.\
\
Students should be verified using an appropriate college email\
domain or an administrator-approved verification process.\
\
Do not assume that every college provides student email addresses.\
\
\
MODULE 2: STUDENT PROFILE MANAGEMENT\
\
Purpose:\
Help students showcase their skills and interests.\
\
Features:\
\
- Student name.\
- Profile picture.\
- College.\
- Department or branch.\
- Academic year.\
- Short biography.\
- Technical skills.\
- Areas of interest.\
- Experience level.\
- GitHub profile.\
- Portfolio URL.\
- Projects created.\
- Projects joined.\
- Availability.\
- Preferred project categories.\
\
Students should be able to edit their profiles.\
\
Private information should not be publicly exposed unnecessarily.\
\
\
MODULE 3: PROJECT CREATION AND MANAGEMENT\
\
Purpose:\
Allow students to publish project ideas and recruit teammates.\
\
Features:\
\
- Create a project.\
- Edit project details.\
- View project details.\
- Delete or archive a project.\
- Specify required skills.\
- Define team size.\
- Specify open roles.\
- Set recruitment deadlines.\
- Define project duration.\
- Select project category.\
- Close recruitment.\
- Manage team membership.\
\
Project fields:\
\
- Project title.\
- Short description.\
- Detailed description.\
- Problem statement.\
- Proposed solution.\
- Technology stack.\
- Required skills.\
- Project category.\
- Project type.\
- Owner.\
- Team size.\
- Current member count.\
- Available roles.\
- Recruitment deadline.\
- Project status.\
- Creation date.\
\
Project categories may include:\
\
- Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning.\
- Web Development.\
- Mobile Application Development.\
- Cybersecurity.\
- Data Science.\
- Internet of Things.\
- Robotics.\
- Blockchain.\
- Research.\
- Other.\
\
Project types may include:\
\
- Mini-project.\
- Major academic project.\
- Personal project.\
- Research project.\
- Hackathon project.\
\
Project statuses:\
\
- Recruiting.\
- Recruitment Closed.\
- In Progress.\
- Completed.\
- Archived.\
\
\
MODULE 4: PROJECT DISCOVERY AND SEARCH\
\
Purpose:\
Help students discover relevant projects.\
\
Features:\
\
- Browse all accessible projects.\
- Search by title.\
- Search by description.\
- Filter by category.\
- Filter by technology.\
- Filter by required skills.\
- Filter by project type.\
- Filter by academic year where appropriate.\
- Sort by newest.\
- Sort by closing date.\
- Display available team positions.\
- Display recruitment status.\
- Bookmark projects.\
- Show recommended projects.\
\
Search results should be paginated when necessary.\
\
Students should not be able to access projects belonging to\
unauthorized college communities.\
\
\
MODULE 5: APPLICATION AND RECRUITMENT MANAGEMENT\
\
Purpose:\
Manage the process of recruiting team members.\
\
Application workflow:\
\
1. Student discovers a project.\
2. Student opens its details.\
3. Student selects an available role.\
4. Student submits an application.\
5. Project owner receives a notification.\
6. Project owner reviews the application.\
7. Project owner accepts or rejects it.\
8. The applicant receives the decision.\
9. Accepted applicants become team members.\
\
Application information:\
\
- Applicant.\
- Project.\
- Requested role.\
- Introduction message.\
- Relevant skills.\
- Application date.\
- Application status.\
\
Application statuses:\
\
- Pending.\
- Accepted.\
- Rejected.\
- Withdrawn.\
\
Features:\
\
- Apply to a project.\
- View submitted applications.\
- Withdraw an application.\
- View application status.\
- Review applicants.\
- View applicant profiles.\
- Accept applicants.\
- Reject applicants.\
- Close applications.\
- Prevent duplicate active applications.\
- Enforce team capacity.\
\
Only authorized project owners or designated managers should be\
able to make recruitment decisions.\
\
Application acceptance and team membership updates must be handled\
safely by the backend or database.\
\
\
MODULE 6: TEAM MANAGEMENT\
\
Purpose:\
Manage students after they join a project.\
\
Features:\
\
- Display team members.\
- Display team roles.\
- View team details.\
- Assign team responsibilities.\
- Allow members to leave a team.\
- Allow authorized owners to remove members.\
- Transfer project ownership where appropriate.\
- Display team capacity.\
- Display project progress.\
\
The project owner should automatically become a team member.\
\
The application must define what happens when the owner leaves\
or transfers ownership.\
\
\
MODULE 7: TEAM COLLABORATION WORKSPACE\
\
Purpose:\
Help accepted members coordinate their work.\
\
Features:\
\
- Project task board.\
- Create tasks.\
- Assign tasks to members.\
- Set task deadlines.\
- Update task status.\
- Add task descriptions.\
- Post team announcements.\
- Share useful links.\
- Share project resources.\
- Display project milestones.\
- Track basic project progress.\
\
Task statuses:\
\
- To Do.\
- In Progress.\
- Completed.\
\
Only authorized project members should be able to access the\
project's private collaboration workspace.\
\
Real-time chat is optional and can be introduced in a later release.\
\
\
MODULE 8: NOTIFICATION SYSTEM\
\
Purpose:\
Inform students about important activities.\
\
Notification events:\
\
- New project application.\
- Application accepted.\
- Application rejected.\
- New team member.\
- Team membership change.\
- New task assignment.\
- Upcoming task deadline.\
- New team announcement.\
- Recruitment status change.\
\
Initial implementation:\
\
- In-app notifications.\
- Read and unread status.\
- Notification timestamps.\
- Notification navigation.\
\
Email notifications can be added later.\
\
\
MODULE 9: BOOKMARKS AND SAVED PROJECTS\
\
Purpose:\
Allow students to save interesting opportunities.\
\
Features:\
\
- Bookmark a project.\
- Remove a bookmark.\
- View saved projects.\
- Open bookmarked project details.\
- Identify projects that are no longer recruiting.\
\
Each student should be able to manage only their own bookmarks.\
\
\
MODULE 10: ADMINISTRATION AND MODERATION\
\
Purpose:\
Maintain a safe and organized student community.\
\
Features:\
\
- View users.\
- Review student verification.\
- Suspend accounts when justified.\
- Review reported projects.\
- Review reported users.\
- Remove inappropriate listings.\
- Manage project categories.\
- View platform statistics.\
- Handle moderation requests.\
\
Administrative actions should be restricted to authorized\
administrators and recorded where appropriate.\
\
Project owners should not automatically receive platform-wide\
administrative privileges.\
\
\
8. OPTIONAL ADVANCED FEATURES\
-----------------------------\
\
These features can be introduced after the MVP is functional.\
\
A. SMART PROJECT RECOMMENDATIONS\
\
Recommend projects based on:\
\
- Student skills.\
- Student interests.\
- Preferred project type.\
- Required skills.\
- Availability.\
- Recruitment status.\
\
The first implementation can use a rule-based matching algorithm.\
\
Machine learning is not required for the initial release.\
\
\
B. TEAM SKILL GAP ANALYSIS\
\
Compare required project skills with the skills represented by\
the existing team.\
\
Example:\
\
Required:\
- Python.\
- Machine Learning.\
- React.\
- PostgreSQL.\
\
Current team:\
- Python.\
- Machine Learning.\
- PostgreSQL.\
\
The platform can highlight the need for a React developer.\
\
This feature can help project owners recruit complementary\
team members.\
\
\
C. FIND A PROJECT PARTNER\
\
Allow students to publish a partner request even when they do not\
have a fully developed project idea.\
\
Fields:\
\
- Project type.\
- Academic year.\
- Interests.\
- Preferred skills.\
- Number of partners needed.\
- Availability.\
- Short introduction.\
\
This feature directly addresses students who need partners for\
major university projects.\
\
\
D. PROJECT SHOWCASE\
\
Allow completed teams to publish:\
\
- Project description.\
- Screenshots.\
- Demo URL.\
- GitHub repository.\
- Technologies used.\
- Team members.\
- Key achievements.\
\
Students can use completed projects as portfolio evidence.\
\
\
E. HACKATHON TEAM FORMATION\
\
Allow students to recruit teammates for hackathons and competitions.\
\
Possible fields:\
\
- Event name.\
- Registration deadline.\
- Required skills.\
- Available roles.\
- Team size.\
- Event URL.\
\
\
F. TEAM COMPATIBILITY\
\
Suggest candidates who fill missing technical roles.\
\
The system should present recommendations as guidance rather\
than guaranteeing that students will work well together.\
\
\
