DATABASE DESIGN REQUIREMENTS\
\
- Use primary keys and foreign keys.\
- Use appropriate unique constraints.\
- Index frequently searched columns.\
- Validate required fields.\
- Prevent duplicate active applications.\
- Enforce team capacity safely.\
- Ensure college access restrictions.\
- Use transactions for operations involving multiple records.\
- Define appropriate deletion and archival rules.\
\
A student should not be able to join a project twice.\
\
A project must not exceed its maximum team size.\
\
The owner should be represented in team membership.\
\
The database must preserve the relationship between projects,\
applications, and accepted team members.\
\
\
10. USER WORKFLOWS\
------------------\
\
WORKFLOW A: STUDENT REGISTRATION\
\
1. Student opens ProjectCollab.\
2. Student registers.\
3. Student verifies their email.\
4. Student completes their profile.\
5. Student adds skills and interests.\
6. Student accesses the project discovery page.\
\
\
WORKFLOW B: CREATE A PROJECT\
\
1. Student selects Create Project.\
2. Student enters project details.\
3. Student specifies required skills.\
4. Student specifies roles and team size.\
5. Student publishes the project.\
6. The project appears in discovery results.\
7. Other students can apply.\
\
\
WORKFLOW C: APPLY TO A PROJECT\
\
1. Student browses projects.\
2. Student selects a suitable project.\
3. Student reads the requirements.\
4. Student selects an available role.\
5. Student submits an introduction message.\
6. The application is stored.\
7. The project owner receives a notification.\
8. The student can track the application status.\
\
\
WORKFLOW D: ACCEPT AN APPLICANT\
\
1. Project owner opens the recruitment dashboard.\
2. Owner reviews the applicant's profile.\
3. Owner checks the requested role.\
4. Owner accepts or rejects the application.\
5. Backend validates the decision and team capacity.\
6. If accepted, team membership is created.\
7. Application status is updated.\
8. Applicant receives a notification.\
9. Recruitment closes when appropriate.\
\
\
WORKFLOW E: TEAM COLLABORATION\
\
1. Accepted student opens My Teams.\
2. Student opens the project workspace.\
3. Team members view announcements.\
4. Members create and assign tasks.\
5. Members update task progress.\
6. The team completes the project.\
7. The project owner marks the project completed.\
8. The team can publish a project showcase.\
\
\
