\
12. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS\
-------------------------\
\
1. Hash passwords securely if authentication is implemented locally.\
\
2. Validate all incoming data.\
\
3. Use parameterized database queries.\
\
4. Protect private routes and API endpoints.\
\
5. Enforce role-based authorization.\
\
6. Restrict access to projects based on college membership.\
\
7. Prevent unauthorized application decisions.\
\
8. Prevent duplicate applications.\
\
9. Enforce team size limits transactionally.\
\
10. Rate-limit sensitive endpoints.\
\
11. Store secrets in environment variables.\
\
12. Do not expose private database credentials to the frontend.\
\
13. Avoid exposing private student information.\
\
14. Implement secure session or token handling.\
\
15. Apply database constraints and access-control rules.\
\
16. Validate uploaded files if file uploads are supported.\
\
17. Implement reporting and moderation capabilities.\
\
18. Test authorization by attempting to access resources belonging\
    to other users.\
\
Security must be enforced on the server, not only through frontend\
visibility controls.\
\
\
